      "text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 1 #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Tropical Cyclone \"PAOLO\"\nIssued at: 8:45 AM, 03 October 2025(Friday)\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Zambales, Bataan, Batangas, Cavite and Quezon(Buenavista, Burdeos, Calauag, Catanauan, General Luna, Guinayangan, Jomalig, Lopez, Macalelon, Mulanay, Panukulan, Patnanungan, Polillo, San Andres, San Francisco, San Narciso, Tagkawayan).\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: Possible FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, expect light to moderate with occasional heavy rains over Metro Manila, Laguna and Pampanga within the next 3 hours.\nLight to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Nueva Ecija, Rizal, Bulacan(Baliuag, Bustos, Dona Remedios Trinidad, Pandi, San Ildefonso, San Miguel, Santa Maria, San Rafael, Angat, Norzagaray, San Jose del Monte), Quezon(Candelaria, Dolores, San Antonio, Sariaya, Tiaong, General Nakar, Tayabas, Infanta, Lucban, Lucena, Mauban, Pagbilao, Real, Sampaloc, Agdangan, Alabat, Atimonan, Gumaca, Padre Burgos, Perez, Pitogo, Plaridel, Quezon, Unisan) and Tarlac(Moncada, Camiling, San Clemente, Paniqui, Anao, San Manuel, Ramos) which may persist within 3 hours and may affect nearby areas.\n\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 11:00 AM today.\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
